YouTube Mix Remover
===================

Stops YouTube from silently turning a normal video click into a Mix queue, while leaving explicitly selected playlists alone.

What it does
------------

- Removes Mix/radio parameters from individual video navigations.
- Preserves normal playlists such as `list=PL...` and playlist position parameters.
- Watches the queue after an “Add to queue” action and removes newly injected Mix items while retaining the selected video and the queue that was already present.
- Runs at document start and uses YouTube's SPA navigation event where available, avoiding the old cancel-and-force-reload approach in the normal case.


What it doesnt do
------------------

- Collect any data whatsoever


Browser support
---------------

The source uses Manifest V3 with both `background.scripts` (Firefox) and `background.service_worker` (Chrome). Firefox currently uses the background script path, while Chromium uses the service worker path.


